1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,160
If every single tree

2
00:00:01,160 --> 00:00:02,680
on Earth vanished overnight,

3
00:00:03,160 --> 00:00:04,140
the planet would quickly

4
00:00:04,140 --> 00:00:05,860
turn into an uninhabitable

5
00:00:05,860 --> 00:00:06,420
wasteland.

6
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:08,940
Trees absorb massive amounts

7
00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:10,720
of carbon dioxide and

8
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:11,800
produce a huge portion

9
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:12,880
of the oxygen we

10
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:13,200
breathe.

11
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:14,760
Without them,

12
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:16,860
greenhouse gases would skyrocket,

13
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:19,100
trapping heat and causing

14
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:20,660
global temperatures to surge

15
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:21,300
rapidly.

16
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:23,520
Tree roots also act

17
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:25,020
like giant underground nets

18
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:26,120
holding soil together.

19
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:27,360
Without them,

20
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:28,940
heavy rains would wash

21
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:30,380
away fertile topsoil,

22
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:32,960
triggering devastating mudslides and

23
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:34,580
turning farmland into barren

24
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:35,020
deserts.

25
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:37,360
Billions of animal species

26
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:38,540
would lose their homes

27
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:40,180
and food sources instantly,

28
00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:42,080
collapsing the entire global

29
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:43,560
food chain and leaving

30
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:45,360
humanity fighting over dwindling

31
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:46,640
oxygen and crops.
